"{"title":"go-readability","description":"go-readability - Readeck fork of github.com/go-shiori/go-readability","url":"[](https://codeberg.org/readeck/go-readability%5C%22,%5C%22content%5C%22:%5C%22Go-Readability)[https://codeberg.org/readeck/go-readability\](https://codeberg.org/readeck/go-readability%5C)",\\"content\\":\\"Go-Readability is a Go package that find the main readable content and the metadata from a HTML page. It works by removing clutter like buttons, ads, background images, script, etc.\n\nThis is a fork of github.com/go-shiori/go-readability originally written by Radhi Fadlillah and maintained by Felipe Martin and GitHub contributors. For more information about the changes in this fork, see FORK.md.\n\nRadhi Fadlillah initially ported Readability.js line-by-line to Go to make sure it looks and works as similar as possible. This way, hopefully all web page that can be parsed by Readability.js are parse-able by go-readability as well.\n\nThis module is compatible with Readability.js v0.6.0.\n\n## Installation\n\n__Note:__ you are viewing documentation for version 0, which is API-compatible with `github.com/go-shiori/go-readability`. The development of this project continues in the v2 branch, which you should choose for *best speed and memory efficiency*, with API-breaking changes being that some `Article` fields were converted to methods.\n\nTo add this package to your project, use `go get`:\n\n`\\ngo get -u codeberg.org/readeck/go-readability\\n`\n\nAnd to get the v2 branch instead:\n\n`\\ngo get -u codeberg.org/readeck/go-readability/v2\\n`\n\n## Example\n\n`\\npackage main\\n\\nimport (\\n\\t\\\"fmt\\\"\\n\\t\\\"log\\\"\\n\\t\\\"os\\\"\\n\\n\\treadability \\\"codeberg.org/readeck/go-readability\\\"\\n)\\n\\nfunc main() {\\n\\tsrcFile, err := os.Open(\\\"index.html\\\")\\n\\tif err != nil {\\n\\t\\tlog.Fatal(err)\\n\\t}\\n\\tdefer srcFile.Close()\\n\\n\\tbaseURL, _ := url.Parse(\\\"https://example.com/path/to/article\\\")\\n\\tarticle, err := readability.FromReader(srcFile, baseURL)\\n\\tif err != nil {\\n\\t\\tlog.Fatal(err)\\n\\t}\\n\\n\\tfmt.Printf(\\\"Found article with title %q\\\\n\\\\n\\\", article.Title)\\n\\t// Print the parsed, cleaned-up HTML markup of the article.\\n\\tfmt.Println(article.Content)\\n}\\n`\n\n## Command Line Usage\n\nYou can also use `go-readability` as command-line tool:\n\n`\\ngo install codeberg.org/readeck/go-readability/cmd/go-readability@latest\\n`\n\nNow you can use it by running `go-readability` in your terminal :\n\n`\\n$ go-readability -h\\n\\ngo-readability is a parser that extracts article contents from a web page.\\nThe source can be a URL or a filesystem path to a HTML file.\\nPass \\\"-\\\" or no argument to read the HTML document from standard input.\\nUse \\\"--http :0\\\" to automatically choose an available port for the HTTP server.\\n\\nUsage:\\n go-readability [<flags>...] [<url> | <file> | -]\\n\\nFlags:\\n -h, --help help for go-readability\\n -l, --http string start the http server at the specified address\\n -m, --metadata only print the page's metadata\\n -t, --text only print the page's text\\n`","metadata":{"og:image":"[](https://codeberg.org/readeck/go-readability/-/summary-card%5C%22,%5C%22og:image:alt%5C%22:%5C%22%E4%BB%93%E5%BA%93)[https://codeberg.org/readeck/go-readability/-/summary-card\](https://codeberg.org/readeck/go-readability/-/summary-card%5C)",\\"og:image:alt\\":\\"仓库 readeck/go-readability 的摘要卡片，描述为：Readeck fork of github.com/go-shiori/go-readability","og:image:width":"1200","og:type":"object","og:site_name":"Codeberg.org","keywords":"git,non-profit,foss,oss,free,software,open,source,code,hosting","author":"readeck","og:title":"go-readability","og:image:height":"600","description":"go-readability - Readeck fork of github.com/go-shiori/go-readability","og:description":"Readeck fork of github.com/go-shiori/go-readability","referrer":"strict-origin","viewport":"width=device-width, initial-scale=1","lang":"zh-CN","og:url":"[](https://codeberg.